---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Builder Pays Either Way | The Precon Market"
  description="Builder co-op commission is paid whether or not you bring your own representation. Walk in without an agent and the builder keeps it."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-4 pt-8 sm:px-6 sm:pt-12">
    <p class="section-label">— Representation</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl">The builder pays for your representation whether you use it or not.</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      <p>
        Most pre-construction projects budget a co-operating commission for the buyer's brokerage. It's built into the
        price. That number doesn't change based on whether you walk into the sales office alone or with your own
        broker.
      </p>
      <p>
        Walk in unrepresented, and that budget doesn't come back to you as a discount — the builder keeps it. You pay
        the same price and get the builder's sales team, whose job is to sell you the builder's inventory on the
        builder's paper.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bring your own representation, and the same money buys you someone on your side of the table: reviewing the
        worksheet, negotiating deposit structure and incentives, flagging the clauses that cost buyers real money at
        closing — assignment restrictions, development charge caps, and the HST rebate language this site's checker
        exists to catch.
      </p>
      <p class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 font-medium text-ink">
        Same price either way. The only question is who the built-in commission works for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <a
        href="/book?source=representation"
        class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center border border-accent bg-accent px-6 font-medium text-white hover:bg-accent/90"
      >
        Book a call before you visit a sales office
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
